{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vTW92aWVzL0hvbGx5d29vZC8yMDIyL1RoZSUyMFllYXIlMjBCZXR3ZWVuJTIwJTI4MjAyMiUyOS8","type":"movie","name":"The Year Between","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/bdnssamVMsNgeqVE5hFC10HVuJo.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/z8Ay36WHx96slztMaQ1smtIFvtW.jpg","description":"Inspired by true events, college sophomore Clemence Miller is coming home to the suburbs and a bedroom in her family's basement. After dropping out of school with a newly diagnosed mental illness, she now faces the challenges of bipolar disorder, the responsibilities of adulthood, and her damaged relationships with family and friends. Clemence struggles to figure out what it means to heal without driving everyone around her… well, crazy. As if reckoning with everything and everyone she has taken for granted wasn’t enough, Clemence has to wrestle with the thought that on top of it all, she might also just have a really bad personality.","releaseInfo":"2022","genres":["Comedy","Drama","Hollywood"],"imdbRating":"4.6","runtime":"94 min","cast":["Alex Heller","J. Smith-Cameron","Steve Buscemi","Emily Robinson","Wyatt Oleff","Kyanna Simone Simpson","Rajeev Jacob","David Brown"],"director":["Alex Heller"],"released":"2023-03-03T00:00:00.000Z","slogan":"Based on real events","app_extras":{"cast":[{"name":"Alex Heller","character":"Clemence","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/wnSRSys7zpsjETzudTac3E1cHll.jpg"},{"name":"J. Smith-Cameron","character":"Sherri","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/7MBc2xJA3BpW3SnDQsww87IA0Tr.jpg"},{"name":"Steve Buscemi","character":"Don","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/n0pZumkrcZrAPMoPq684RhYnjPV.jpg"},{"name":"Emily Robinson","character":"Carlin","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/vbntgPj3bXKI0XA69nMt7Li5MhC.jpg"},{"name":"Wyatt Oleff","character":"Neil","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/wEka1IzC5OtkKGGhlMmItAfDUqW.jpg"},{"name":"Kyanna Simone Simpson","character":"Beth","ph